INT. FLOATING MARKET - INSIDE THE GIANT'S RIBCAGE - DUSK

Lantern-boats drift between enormous curved bones the color of old piano keys. Stalls hang from them on ropes. Fog moves along the waterway.

QUILL (30s, lean, ink-stained fingers, a satchel of maps) haggles at a stall hung with dried fish. SABRA (20s, scarred cheek, hand always near a short knife) leans on a bone. THORN (50s, barrel-chested, a pipe in his teeth) squats on the boat's stern and feeds a pair of ravens.

A HOODED WOMAN (age unknowable, gray cloak) sits by herself at the edge of the water, a single candle at her knee.

QUILL
Eight silver for the lot.

SABRA
You said six.

QUILL
The price changed when the fog came in.

THORN
The fog came in at noon.

HOODED WOMAN
(to no one)
It rises. It does not come in.

They all turn. Sabra's hand tightens on the knife.

SABRA
Who are you?

HOODED WOMAN
Zephyrine.

QUILL
Just Zephyrine?

ZEPHYRINE
Just. It has been enough for six hundred years.

THORN
(low)
Quill. Sabra. We should go.

ZEPHYRINE
You have a map of the Ember Coast. I would very much like to see it.

Quill's hand goes to his satchel. The ravens lift off the boat in a rush of black wings. Thorn rises, pipe falling from his teeth.

A new shadow crosses the water. GRIMBOLD (40s, stooped, wearing a toll-keeper's brass chain, his lantern held very high) steps onto the stall's plank and looks at them all with weary patience.

GRIMBOLD
Toll.

SABRA
We paid at the gate.

GRIMBOLD
That was the gate. This is the rib.

THORN
(dual with Quill)
You can't charge for bones, you old thief.

QUILL
^You can't charge for a bone, it's the whole market.

GRIMBOLD
Bones belong to the dead. The dead pay me.

ZEPHYRINE
(rising)
Then let them pay for me, Grimbold. I am not here for the toll.

Grimbold's lantern wavers. The candle at her knee gutters out. For a long beat nobody speaks. Then the old man bows, very slightly, and steps aside.

GRIMBOLD
Mistress.

ZEPHYRINE
(to Quill)
The map.

Quill hands it over. Sabra exhales. Thorn retrieves his pipe from the planks and, with great care, does not relight it.
